    "extraction_notes": [
      "The supplied datasheet publishes output, transfer, on-resistance, and capacitance plots on p. 3; curve points are digitized readings from visible traces without interpolation between unobserved samples.",
      "Transfer-curve values were converted from the plotted mA axis to A, and capacitance-curve values were converted from pF to F.",
      "The supplied tables publish no typical threshold value, body-diode forward-voltage value, gate-charge value, reverse-recovery value, or junction-to-case thermal resistance. The only thermal resistance published is typical RthetaJA=625 degC/W on p. 1, which has no field in the supplied schema.",
      "The Fig. 1 upper current label is rendered as 1.5 in the supplied scan; the plotted grid, 0.1 A drain-current rating, and visible curves indicate an upper plotted range of approximately 0.15 A. The 3.5 V and 4.0 V traces leave that plotted range and are recorded only over their visible portions."
    ],
